erator change.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.075,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Testing: 'verify `docs/config-reference.md` does not drift unexpectedly from the scanner documentation generator change'","AC7 covers regenerated `docs/security.md` only; no AC mentions `docs/config-reference.md`"],"finding":"The Testing section requires verifying that `docs/config-reference.md` does not drift unexpectedly from the scanner documentation-generator change, but no acceptance criterion covers this config-reference no-drift regression guard.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f7c764eb660fd776d","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Testing ('verify docs/config-reference.md does not drift unexpectedly') vs Acceptance Criteria","norm_id":"n805f027b3b00f4dc","priority":0.875,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The scanner gen change alters config-reference output as a side effect and it lands unnoticed because no AC asserts no-drift"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"missing_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Declare the new `gerrit-scanner-verify.yml` advisory workflow's least-privilege posture: an explicit minimal `permissions:` block (e.g. contents: read only), no repository secrets exposed to jobs that run patchset code, and no write scope — mirroring the read-only posture of gerrit-verify.yaml.","cohort":["T5c"],"criteria":["T5c"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.025,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'a separate Gerrit exact-patchset advisory workflow (.github/workflows/gerrit-scanner-verify.yml)' dispatched on 'patchset events'","gerrit-verify.yaml declares `permissions: contents: read / actions: read / checks: read` as its explicit read-only posture (lines 46-49)","ABSENCE: the plan never states the advisory workflow's `permissions` block or that it withholds secrets; untrusted patchset code executing in CI is the boundary, so the posture should be declared even though no secret asset is affirmatively introduced (minor/advisory per AMBIGUOUS-reachability fallback)"],"finding":"The plan introduces a new Gerrit advisory workflow (.github/workflows/gerrit-scanner-verify.yml) that is dispatched on patchset-created and therefore checks out and executes lower-trust contributor patchset code in CI, but the plan does not declare the workflow's least-privilege posture (its `permissions:` block, and that it holds no secrets/write scope). The sibling gerrit-verify.yaml explicitly scopes itself to contents:read/actions:read/checks:read; the new lane crossing the same untrusted-code boundary should state an equivalent minimal, secret-free posture so a compromised patchset cannot reach voting credentials or write scopes.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc193700226cf4010","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Advisory wiring constraint / Scope (`.github/workflows/gerrit-scanner-verify.yml`)","norm_id":"n819b1